From ecfbc8bc2f0b2c50f637877053932f8f2bed8cbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:48:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add text animation and UI shaders to the widget UI

Text animation (UIText):
- reveal: Typewriter / Fade / Pop / Rise / Drop / Spin, with speed,
  delay, per-character fade time, sound every N characters, restart on
  show, and a manual revealProgress (0-1) for timelines
- effect: Wave / Shake / Rainbow / Pulse / Swing / Glitch
- inline tags: <wave> <shake> <rainbow> <pulse> <swing> <glitch>
  <color=#RRGGBB(AA)> <alpha=x> <pause=sec> <speed=x>; unknown tags stay
  as text, and tags are left out of the measured size
- RestartReveal / SkipReveal / IsRevealing, UIEventType::TextRevealed,
  UIDocument::RestartText / SkipText / IsTextRevealing
- characters are drawn one quad each so every glyph can move

UI shaders:
- .uishader assets: one GLSL effect(vec4 color) function with helpers
  (uTime, uRect, LocalUV, SampleTexture, Luma, HueShift, Noise) and up
  to 6 "// @param" values (float / vec2 / color / toggle)
- every widget gets shader, shaderChildren and shaderParam0-5 (only
  saved when a shader is set; animatable like other properties)
- nested shaders, fallback to normal drawing on compile errors, error
  lines numbered as in the .uishader, hot reload when the file changes
- 13 presets (grayscale, sepia, flash, shine, dissolve, gradient,
  rainbow, hue shift, blink, scanlines, hologram, vignette, wave)
- Renderer2D::SetShader for custom fragment shaders; Shader keeps its
  error log; AssetType::UIShader and the editor's asset list

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
